Minimal fail-to-pass extraction for openhwgroup/cve2 PR 139, "move nmi to irq
32".

The reduced IRQ cause/vector logic models the real diff: fast interrupts expand
from 15 to 16 inputs, exception causes expand from 6 to 7 bits, fast IRQ15 uses
cause 31, and NMI moves to cause 32.  The buggy snapshot still encodes NMI as
the old cause 31 and ignores fast IRQ15.  The Verilator testbench drives NMI
and fast IRQ15 and checks both cause and vector address.

